Advanced Thermodynamics — MIT 2.43, Spring 2024 (@th-beretta: 0, is #reference, #part-of @th-sources) { r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC
Gian Paolo Beretta. MIT 2.43 Advanced Thermodynamics, Spring 2024, graduate. [Course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-43-advanced-thermodynamics-spring-2024/) · [Syllabus and assessment](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-43-advanced-thermodynamics-spring-2024/pages/syllabus/).

Complete the public lecture/slides progression, its assignment and explanatory examination work. It connects rigorous general thermodynamics with multicomponent and electrochemical equilibrium, reaction affinity, separation/mixing, metastability and near-equilibrium coupled transport. Reconstruct assumptions and derivations, then compare them with [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1) and [The physics and mathematics of the second law — Lieb and Yngvason](Second-Law-Foundations-Lieb-Yngvason.lingua#r_4ZBR10NAYWD4G8ZJYQV7PXS8DZ).

The syllabus has one conventional homework assignment, four explanatory take-home quizzes and an oral final, rather than a large numerical problem-set archive. Our numerical and experimental studies complement that actual course. MIT OCW uses CC BY-NC-SA with exceptions for separately credited material and external readings; a public course does not make every cited commercial textbook open. All materials remain links.

**Return:** [Thermodynamics and heat transfer sources](../Sources.lingua#r_4N96T70VYW3C3M91M2SXF5KEQF).
